1
00:00:00,750 --> 00:00:03,700
This tour shows the ways to start a fit,

2
00:00:03,700 --> 00:00:07,663
and how OFE-GUI and OFE-Go
run many fits at once.

3
00:00:07,813 --> 00:00:11,472
It uses one real
field-cycling NMR measurement:

4
00:00:11,472 --> 00:00:16,416
44 relaxation curves, from 8
megahertz down to 3 kilohertz.

5
00:00:17,916 --> 00:00:20,137
There are three ways to start a fit.

6
00:00:20,287 --> 00:00:23,021
A model expression with data files,

7
00:00:23,171 --> 00:00:27,797
a saved fit, in JSON or
the older SAV format,

8
00:00:27,947 --> 00:00:30,644
or a batch of fits that run in parallel.

9
00:00:30,794 --> 00:00:38,033
In OFE-GUI each is a tab or a button;
in OFE-Go, the arguments of onefite fit.

10
00:00:39,533 --> 00:00:42,823
First, a model and data:
the model expression,

11
00:00:42,823 --> 00:00:46,821
with starting values and
limits, and the data file.

12
00:00:46,971 --> 00:00:49,661
This Stelar file holds all 44 curves;

13
00:00:49,661 --> 00:00:53,573
each becomes a data block,
tagged with its field.

14
00:00:53,723 --> 00:00:59,100
--individual fits every block on its
own: one line of results per block.

15
00:00:59,250 --> 00:01:03,705
--save-to writes the
whole fit to t005.json.

16
00:01:05,205 --> 00:01:09,719
In OFE-GUI, that is the Function
+ data files tab: the model,

17
00:01:09,719 --> 00:01:13,696
and the Stelar file,
uploaded from this computer.

18
00:01:13,846 --> 00:01:19,015
The fit mode is Individual, and Save
engine description names the JSON file.

19
00:01:19,165 --> 00:01:23,626
Plots shows every block's fit,
and Output lists the 44 results.

20
00:01:23,776 --> 00:01:30,104
T1 grows from 2.00 seconds at 3
kilohertz to 3.29 seconds at 8 megahertz.

21
00:01:30,254 --> 00:01:33,433
In the Terminal: this
server has four CPUs,

22
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:36,592
and the saved file has 44 DATA blocks.

23
00:01:38,092 --> 00:01:40,783
The saved JSON describes the whole fit.

24
00:01:40,933 --> 00:01:43,494
Function and Parameters hold the model,

25
00:01:43,494 --> 00:01:47,849
with each parameter's value,
limits, and fixed or free state.

26
00:01:47,999 --> 00:01:52,809
Dados holds the data. Each block
starts with a DATA line and a TAG line,

27
00:01:52,809 --> 00:01:54,161
which names it.

28
00:01:54,311 --> 00:01:57,509
The DATA line gives the
block its own values of T,

29
00:01:57,509 --> 00:02:01,761
the per-block variable, here
called dum: the field, in hertz.

30
00:02:01,911 --> 00:02:05,763
Tags lists the blocks to fit,
and FitType remembers the mode.

31
00:02:07,263 --> 00:02:12,185
In OFE-GUI, the JSON/SAV/Jobs
tab takes saved fits,

32
00:02:12,185 --> 00:02:15,815
and Edit shows one field by field.

33
00:02:15,965 --> 00:02:18,002
Click a field to edit it.

34
00:02:18,152 --> 00:02:21,251
To rename T, Shift+T opens it on one line;

35
00:02:21,251 --> 00:02:25,659
the new name is carried into
the model and every block.

36
00:02:25,809 --> 00:02:30,805
Write All in Tags, and saving puts
in the tag of every block in Dados.

37
00:02:32,305 --> 00:02:34,677
OFE-Go fits a saved file directly,

38
00:02:34,677 --> 00:02:38,516
starting from its saved
values, in its saved mode.

39
00:02:38,666 --> 00:02:43,119
--selected-dataset fits some
of its blocks, for one run:

40
00:02:43,119 --> 00:02:47,127
by tag, by position, or
a range such as #1-#4.

41
00:02:47,277 --> 00:02:53,580
In OFE-GUI, that is Selected data sets,
where all picks every block of the file.

42
00:02:53,730 --> 00:02:58,560
A SAV file fits the same way,
and convert turns it into JSON.

43
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:03,506
A batch runs many complete
fits with one command.

44
00:03:03,656 --> 00:03:07,589
A jobs file has one fit per
line: a model and its data,

45
00:03:07,589 --> 00:03:10,943
or a saved fit, each with its own options.

46
00:03:11,093 --> 00:03:15,029
Here: the same data with two
models, fitted individually,

47
00:03:15,029 --> 00:03:17,796
and the saved fit, fitted globally.

48
00:03:17,946 --> 00:03:22,179
--jobs sets how many fits run
at once. Each fit gets its own

49
00:03:22,179 --> 00:03:24,225
folder in a new batch folder,

50
00:03:24,225 --> 00:03:26,832
and batch.json records them all.

51
00:03:26,982 --> 00:03:32,477
If one fit fails, the others keep running.
Several saved fits run the same way.

52
00:03:33,977 --> 00:03:38,387
In OFE-GUI, Jobs edits
a jobs file as a table.

53
00:03:38,537 --> 00:03:43,012
Models × data adds a row for every
model line on every data file,

54
00:03:43,012 --> 00:03:46,872
and each row can have its
own fit mode and options.

55
00:03:47,022 --> 00:03:50,151
Save and use makes it the
input of the next fit.

56
00:03:50,301 --> 00:03:53,941
Fits at once is 2, so
two fits run together.

57
00:03:54,091 --> 00:03:59,267
The Fits bar shows each fit's state and
chi-square, and Output the whole batch.

58
00:03:59,417 --> 00:04:03,893
Click a fit to see its plots
and parameters. The global fit,

59
00:04:03,893 --> 00:04:07,675
one T1 for every field,
can't follow the data:

60
00:04:07,825 --> 00:04:13,740
its chi-square is 41, against
0.048 for the individual fits.

61
00:04:15,240 --> 00:04:17,883
Fits run in parallel at two levels.

62
00:04:18,033 --> 00:04:18,962
Inside one fit,

63
00:04:18,962 --> 00:04:22,246
the blocks of an individual
fit run at the same time,

64
00:04:22,246 --> 00:04:25,447
and so do the per-block
parts of a hybrid fit.

65
00:04:25,597 --> 00:04:29,478
--workers caps how many, at
the number of CPUs by default,

66
00:04:29,478 --> 00:04:32,639
and --no-parallel runs them one at a time.

67
00:04:32,789 --> 00:04:41,329
Across fits, a batch runs --jobs fits
at once, as many as the CPUs by default.

68
00:04:41,479 --> 00:04:44,563
Each fit then gets its share of the CPUs:

69
00:04:44,563 --> 00:04:48,899
four CPUs and two fits at
once give two workers each.

70
00:04:49,049 --> 00:04:53,112
Parallel fits need the engine
on OFE-GUI's own machine:

71
00:04:53,112 --> 00:04:56,343
your computer, or the server with -ssh.

72
00:04:57,843 --> 00:05:03,396
Model and data, saved fits, and
batches: three ways in, one engine.

73
00:05:03,546 --> 00:05:09,154
onefite man describes every option,
and Help does the same in OFE-GUI.

74
